// Transcription of ~/dev/system/base/parseraddition.pas — the WSM BUILDER the
// parser drives.
//
// The original declares three abstract stacks in syntax.pas (BlockObj / ItemObj
// / SubexpObj, all methods empty) and ONE concrete descendant of each here.
// Because the override set is closed and has exactly one member, the port
// flattens the virtual dispatch: every `gSubexpPtr^.Foo` in the grammar becomes
// a call to `mizSubFoo(p)` and the abstract no-op bodies simply have no
// counterpart. The three stacks themselves are kept — they are real state.
//
// The unit's file-level `var`s (gLastTerm, gLastType, TermNbr, Term, gPattern,
// …) become fields of MizParser, the one per-article state record, as the
// CONVENTIONS require. Their names are kept.
//
// ★ THE TERM STACK IS THE HEART OF IT. Every visible argument is pushed onto
//   `Term` by FinishArgument and popped in bulk by CreateArgs(base), which
//   truncates the stack. Index 0 is unused — the Pascal array is written to at
//   Term[TermNbr] with TermNbr starting at 0 and pre-incremented.

import ds/vector;
import loop;
import string;
import mizar/original/errhan;
import mizar/original/scanner;
import mizar/original/formats;
import mizar/original/wsm;

